                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The concept of this game is great especially for anyone looking for a simulation style game in the world of drugs and drug empires.  I came to this game from Cartel Tycoon and, for the first couple of hours, had a lot of fun.  Unfortunately the game is on rails with some very stringent rules come level 4 or so.  As an example, you sometimes can take out some enemies but can't take them out \"too much\" (even if they are your competition).  In level 4 you have to make sure both of your competitors are alive simultaneously and are not allowed to take either out completely (you have to leave one and exactly one of each of their buildings all while juggling watching their moving vehicles and creating your own drug empire).  It's because of the rails that it really makes the game not fun very quickly as it doesn't matter how good your empire is going, how much money you have, and how strong your group is; if there isn't a certain number of enemies at all times, you instantly lose the level.\r\n\r\nAs an alternative, if you want more freedom, there is the Sandbox mode that is not on rails but once you eliminate the enemies on that map the fun basically ends.  You can grow your empire but, very quickly, you grow it enough and your only real option is just to start over from scratch again.  \r\n\r\nAll in all, it's not a terrible game but probably not worth the full MSRP.  Waiting for a sale where you can grab it for 5-10 dollars USD is probably the most I would say the game is worth as I found myself completely burnt out of playing it 20 hours in.",
